=== zone gz10g
Tunnel
The tunnel is just another relic of ancient times, like other numerous Gipath ruins. Once upon a time it was the shortest and safest way through the mountains and into the ravine, but a lot has changed since then.

=== zone gz11k
City environs
There is only one city in this province of Ingos; it is the seat of the government. The people in the surrounding villages are hostile to the citizens because of the ruinous decrees of the governor. The woods around are populated by creatures called "Woodsfolk". Their interests rarely coincide with these of humans.

=== zone gz12k
Abandoned mines
A long time ago this area was famous for its mining industry. But they closed the mines when monsters and ogres started to appear and the area   deteriorated. Now the very few people who live in this territory do not feel they have any obligation to the city government.

=== zone gz13k
Karansul's domain
Here one can find numerous workshops owned by the merchant Karansul. His lieutenants control almost the whole area except the narrow valleys between the mountain spurs. A while ago there was a laboratory of Canian Warrior Magicians here, but after one of their usual miscalculations these valleys became lethal.

=== zone gz14k
Forbidden catacombs
When the miners disturbed the lairs of the subterranean creatures, gold and stone mining stopped. Soon all the drifts and galleries overflowed with monsters, forcing the governor to close the mine completely.

=== zone gz15h
Death canyon
A Khadaganian army training camp is located here. Soldiers who are working on promotions hunt prisoners whom are kept in a separate dungeon.

=== zone gz16h
Wormheads' cave
A deep cave with a Wormheads' Temple in it - these are creatures with strong magic abilities. To try and clean out the cave would mean heavy casualties, so the Khadaganian military simply guard the exits.

=== zone gz17h
Necromancers' desert
Necromancers' homes and laboratories are located in the desert, away from prying eyes. The barracks of the guards responsible for the security of these installations are also located here.

=== zone gz18h
The city of Suslanger and its environs
The city which gives its name to all of the surrounding lands is located on the lake shore. Numerous irrigation canals flow from the lake. The people who work the fields are not armed, but they would certainly raise the alarm as soon as they saw a stranger -  they would be punished otherwise.

=== zone gz19h
Portal
Though Suslangers call Gipath "The Useless Lands", the portal is closely guarded.

=== zone gz1g
Ruins
This territory got its name from the ruins of ancient structures. While it is relatively safe, you may find yourself in a very uncomfortable situation should you lose your way.

=== zone gz20g
Catacombs
This is where the final battle with the Joons' Curse is going to take place!

=== zone gz2g
The road to the Witch
Estera the Witch quarrelled with the whole village and moved into the cave, just to put some distance between herself and other beings. To protect her privacy, she installed a number of magic traps on the road to the cave. And she also uses nearby Trolls for additional protection.

=== zone gz3g
Foothills
Foothills is the frontier between the territory civilized by humans and the wild lands. There is a settlement of "Free Hunters" here, but you have a much better chance of meeting up with Goblins and Orcs than with humans.

=== zone gz4g
Remote Mountains
This is the most remote area from the village. Humans are rare guests here, and occasions where they make it back alive are even rarer still. However, there is a rumor in the village that the Craftsman somehow found out how to reach the stone site located there.

=== zone gz5g
Cave
A large catacomb with several exits on the surface. Even the tough Orcs only managed to bring a small part of the cave under control, and they will not risk venturing into its depths where strange and unfamiliar creatures dwell.

=== zone gz6g
Middle Mountains
These mountains occupy the northern half of the area; the southern half is flatter and easier to traverse. The plains area is sparsely populated, so a cautious traveller could cross it without encountering a single enemy. The mountains are much more dangerous, so humans try to avoid them.

=== zone gz7g
The river and the islands
The river which starts in the Remote Mountains flows into the Big Lake and forms a delta containing numerous islands. There are big Goblin and Orc settlements here, with houses and shrines. "Free hunters" also venture here, but they don't hang around too long.

=== zone gz8g
Sands
East of the Big Lake, there is a sand desert whose northern sector ends in mountainous terrain. Several Orc tribes live there; this is also the main  habitat of the Lizards. Orcs and Lizards compete constantly for access to water.

=== zone gz9g
Dead City
Two mountain ranges jut out on the wide plain and form a valley between. In this valley lies the Dead City which was once populated by humans, but only ghouls nest there now.

